WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.900
Once upon a time, TV shows weren't allowed
to even show married couples sleeping in the

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.009
same bed.

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:07.009
Nowadays?

00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:09.840
You can't go five minutes without seeing a
love scene on TV.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:15.300
But while some love scenes are truly hot,
others just amp the cringe factor up to a

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:16.300
million.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.279
Here's a look at the most awkward on-screen
love scenes in TV.

00:00:20.279 --> 00:00:21.339
Cougar Town

00:00:21.339 --> 00:00:25.259
If you're going to call a show Cougar Town,
you need to have some cougars in it.

00:00:25.259 --> 00:00:29.349
Still, even though actor Dan Byrd is only
six years younger than star Busy Phillips

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:32.700
in real life, this tryst felt really creepy.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:37.430
That's because his character is the son of
her character's best friend, played by Courtney

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:40.700
Cox — who walks in on them together in the
shower.

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.490
Ah.. that's just gross.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:44.490
Friends

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:47.740
Cox has been on the other side of an awkward
love scene, too.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.780
On Friends, she played Monica, who in a sixth
season episode set out to prove that being

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:55.720
sick isn't going to stop her from having a
good time.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:00.470
She aggressively attempts to seduce her reluctant
boyfriend Chandler, finally getting her way

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:04.759
by using that age old aphrodisiac — Vick's
Vapo Rub.

00:01:04.759 --> 00:01:05.759
Oh Yea….

00:01:05.759 --> 00:01:06.759
"Okay.

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.660
If you really want to have it."

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:09.660
"Oh!"

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.020
"Worked like a charm!"

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.060
Ah..

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:14.110
Nope.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:15.789
That '70s Show

00:01:15.789 --> 00:01:19.840
Walking in on your parents is a classic sitcom
joke these days.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:24.259
In That 70's Show, for instance, Eric comes
home when he shouldn't have and walks right

00:01:24.259 --> 00:01:28.429
into his parents' room while they're going
at it like a couple of teenage rabbits.

00:01:28.429 --> 00:01:33.189
Viewers don't see Kitty and Red in the buff,
as the scene unfolds entirely in the form

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:36.389
of Eric's horrified and confused face.

00:01:36.389 --> 00:01:37.939
Two and a Half Men

00:01:37.939 --> 00:01:42.479
Charlie seemed to be the brother who got the
fun and glamorous adult fun times on Two and

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:45.869
a Half Men, while Alan got the difficult ones.

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:51.109
Like the time he ate just a few too many oysters
right as he and girlfriend Lyndsey were about

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:54.130
to get it on during a romantic hotel getaway.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:55.740
Talk about a mood killer.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:56.980
"You don't want to hear what's about to happen!"

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:07.380
It's not just real love that can go horribly
wrong — love over the Internet can glitch

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:08.380
out, too.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:13.310
Just ask Big Bang Theory's Leonard, who attempted
to use his best seductive voice during an

00:02:13.310 --> 00:02:16.500
erotic FaceTime with his girlfriend in India.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:20.840
One problem: her parents were in the room
offscreen and heard every bit of it.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.860
Whoops!

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:23.590
Felicity

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:27.800
The college-set series Felicity was about
a bunch of young adults trying their hardest

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:30.280
to grow up — and often failing.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:34.610
In the first season, the virginal Felicity
returns to school after winter break and tells

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:39.530
her sort-of-boyfriend Noel that she thinks
they should make love for the first time.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:44.220
Leading up to the big night, Felicity gets
very type A, responsible, and practical about

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:48.490
the whole thing, which includes buying books
about love and determining the right form

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:49.490
of birth control.

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:56.860
But when it actually happens, it doesn't quite
happen, thanks to one very poorly placed candle.

00:02:56.860 --> 00:02:57.860
Seinfeld

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:03.150
In a classic episode of Seinfeld, Jerry brags
that Elaine never had to fake it with him—to

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:06.150
which she responds that, well, she did.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:11.260
Jerry begs her for 30 minutes to prove himself,
which she declines because it will "ruin the

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.260
friendship."

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:16.940
When Jerry continues moping, she then changes
her mind for the sake of saving their friendship.

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:21.590
It concludes with a shot of Jerry and Elaine
lying in bed, with Elaine reading a magazine

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:23.400
and Jerry looking crushed.

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:25.070
Oh well.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.670
How I Met Your Mother

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:31.280
On the hit series How I Met Your Mother, Barney's
brother points out the many similarities between

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.190
Barney's new girlfriend Nora and their mom.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:38.750
The thought gets into Barney's head, too,
and before long he keeps seeing his mother

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.170
when he looks at Nora.

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:46.070
Nora eventually initiates things with Barney
on the couch — but he, and the audience,

00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:48.110
sees Mom lying on top of him.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:50.940
There's really only one appropriate reaction
to that...

00:03:50.940 --> 00:03:51.860
"No!

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:52.860
God!

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:55.860
No God Please no.

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:56.920
No!"

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.200
Thanks for watching!

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:00.780
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.760
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

